# Fork desktop releases (local + GitHub)

When building or publishing a desktop release for the **fork** (`teteusantosgd/t3code`), not upstream:

1. After a successful new version lands (local `release/` artifacts and/or a GitHub release on the fork), **keep only the two most recent versions**. Delete older ones.
2. **Local artifacts:** prune `release/T3-Code-*` (and `*.blockmap`, `builder-debug.yml`) so only the latest two version prefixes remain.
3. **App backups:** also prune versioned `.app` copies under `~/t3-backup-*` (e.g. `T3 Code (Alpha) <version>.app`) and `/Applications/T3 Code (Alpha).app.bak`, keeping only the two newest versioned apps. Do **not** delete userdata in those folders (`state.sqlite`, `secrets`, settings, logs).
4. **GitHub fork:** `gh release delete <old-tag> -R teteusantosgd/t3code --yes --cleanup-tag` for tags older than the latest two.
5. Do **not** delete upstream (`pingdotgg/t3code`) releases.
6. Do this cleanup as part of finishing the release work — do not leave old DMGs/EXEs/app backups accumulating on disk.
